name: lag-has-no-value-until-primed
why: lag(x,1) is the value one sample ago; the first sample has no prior, so it emits nothing. 10,20,30 → t2=10 (prior of 20), t3=20 (prior of 30).
expr: lag(nodeA.price, 1)
keys: nodeA.price
resolve: LOCF
--- LOG ---
---
#00:00:01.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 1
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 10.0}
---
#00:00:02.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 2
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 20.0}
---
#00:00:03.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 3
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 30.0}
--- EXPECT ---
2 => 10.0
3 => 20.0
